Z||000022||Phil||11-15-1999||08:46 AM||||haven't heard of grits to stop leaks but I have heard of using a raw egg for a temp fix. But now back to the subject at hand. My son's 88 GT keeps eating up alt/water pump belts about every 5000 mi. The pulleys seem to be in good shape (no nicks,dents etc.) and as far as I can tell they seem to be aligned. I checked them as well as I could with a straight edge. He just blew another one last night, all that's left is some rubber "lint". Any ideas on the cause?||||reg||1
Z||000023||theogre||11-15-1999||10:38 AM||||sounds like they aren't adjusted right, likely to tight. Could also be the belts your buying. are they all from the same source? try another brand.||||reg||1
